{"study_accession":"PRJNA730788","secondary_study_accession":"SRP320303","title":"peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) of pre- and post-treatment periodontitis patients and healthy donors by single-cell RNA profiling","description":"The pathogenic determinants of chronic periodontitis leading to extra-oral comorbidity are unclear. This study was conducted to investigate the main determinants that correlate chronic periodontitis and systemic diseases via periodontitis-evoked molecular changes in immune cells resolved by therapy. Single-cell RNA sequencing using peripheral blood mononuclear cells was performed to compare the molecular and biological differences in immune cells of 4 pre- and 4 post-treatment patients and 4 healthy donors. Periodontal treatment was one-day full-arch scaling and root planning for full mouth disinfection. Altered expression of genes involved in the inflammatory response in the patients was compared with that in healthy donors following therapeutic intervention. The common representative genes across diverse cell types were investigated; those genes were associated with periodontitis-pathogenic bacterial systemic diseases. These important factors correlating chronic periodontitis and systemic inflammatory diseases at the single-cell level may serve as therapeutic targets. Overall design: Single-cell RNA-seq analysis of peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs). samples: 4 healthy and paired pre- and post treatment samples from 4 periodontitis patients.","pubmed":"36329504","geo_series":"","n_samples":12,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN19241259","study_accession":"PRJNA730788","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"Post1","description":"Post1","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5320467","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-11-12","attributes":[["source_name","PBMC_post-treatment"],["subject status","periodontitis patient"],["timepoint","post-treatment"],["cell_type","PBMC"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR